      "source": [
        "# Lock\n",
        "\n",
        "A lock is a synchronization primitive that controls concurrent access to shared resources. A thread typically acquires it before accessing protected state and releases it afterwards.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-lock)"
      ]
    }
